docker/README.md Quick start says `mkdir -m 700 secrets` (owned by the user); handbook ch2 makes the secrets directory root-owned 0700 (`sudo install -d -m 0700 -o root`). Not wrong for lab mode, but a newcomer (walkthrough round 4) saw a contradiction. Fix: one sentence in docker/README pointing at ch2 for a real CA. docker/ = worker lane.

Also: handbook ch2 now carries the CA part on a separate transfer medium (/media/transfer) so the root-key medium never enters the CA host (walkthrough round 5). docker/README.md lines ~336, 493, 523 still use /media/offline/for-the-ca and /media/offline/new-intermediate on the CA host; align them.

